    "measurementTechnique": [
      "The development of the location metadata reporting format was motivated by researchers' need to describe discrete point locations used in various research projects. Because this ESS-DIVE reporting format began after development of 10 other environmental reporting formats, we were able to leverage existing ESS-DIVE metadata recommendations from all relevant reporting formats. We also reviewed and incorporated elements from existing data standards, conventions, and other types of data resources (e.g., Federal Geographic Data Committee, DarwinCore, and the Open Geospatial Consortium's Observation and Measurements standard."
    ],
